  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> and let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be the vertices of a parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt></math> and the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> lie on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to</p>"
